<title>BOTSWANA: BA strike affects flights from Botswana.</title>
<headline>BA strike affects flights from Botswana.</headline>
<dateline>GABORONE 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Airways Plc said on Friday disruption caused by a strike by cabin crew had forced it to re-route passengers travelling from Gaborone to London on August 16, 23 and 30.</p>
<p>Botswana manager Julian Huxtable said passengers would be   flown by a</p>
<p>chartered carrier to Johannesburg to connect with flights from South Africa.</p>
<p>&quot;We have come to agreements with one of the two cabin crew unions, but are still negotiating with the other,&quot; Huxtable said.</p>
<p>Passengers will connect with the regular BA 747 service at Johannesburg.</p>
<p>BA's Monday services from Gaborone to London will not be affected.</p>
<p>Huxtable said he expected the situation to return to normal at the beginning of September.</p>
